      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e It seems better to just do both kvm_topup_pkvm_memcache() and kzalloc() before calling kvm_mmu_faultin_pfn()?\n\nHmm, OTOH it means that e.g. in case of MMIO emulation for npVM (i.e. a normal scenario, not a failure path), we needlessly top up the memcache and allocate struct pkvm_mapping only to free it right after that...\n\n...So maybe let\u0027s release the refcounted page, but do it by directly calling kvm_release_faultin_page() with unused\u003dtrue instead of kvm_mmu_finish_page_fault(), to avoid confusion?\n\nBTW just noticed this inside kvm_release_faultin_page():\n\n```\n\tlockdep_assert_once(lockdep_is_held(\u0026kvm-\u003emmu_lock) || unused);\n```\n\nso it looks like it is indeed safe to do it without holding mmu_lock.",
      "parentUuid": "65b30fcb_0288df76",
      "revId": "797a7099b6de02916da49b3e19050081a7ff81d3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
